+# KAI offline preflight scope
+
+This candidate continues batch001 over aictrl-dev/skills commit
+`d4b42bf96f550e427a16a5ac7b5f40117cb26963`. It retains that complete skill
+unit and MIT license. The inspected js-yaml 4.3.2 runtime is pinned inside
+`vendor/js-yaml`; it does not import the host's YAML package. Ajv 8.20.0 and
+ajv-formats 3.0.1 remain required in an isolated host toolchain.
+
+The schema is unchanged. Additional local checks reject retries above zero
+(the guide says apply rejects them), absent node IDs, cyclic YAML aliases,
+non-finite values and excessive input complexity. Three nested loops and an
+iteration product of 1000 are allowed; four levels or a greater product are
+rejected. Cycle detection is iterative. A malformed schema instance never
+enters graph traversal. Input is limited to a regular file of 1 MiB, parser
+depth 64, 100,000 visited values and a merge budget of 1000. JSON_SCHEMA does
+not expand YAML merge keys or construct custom tags.
+
+Exit 0 proves only the stated local structural/static checks. It does not
+prove that a skill/template exists in an organisation or that a workflow is
+publishable, executable, safe to run, or correct. No network/apply is performed.
+
+Not checked: CEL syntax/typing/evaluation; input parameter existence; required
+task inputs and static input type compatibility; gate existence/type/wave
+ordering; whether an existing node output is available before it is consumed;
+organisation permissions, effects, budgets and credentials. JSON duplicate
+keys retain JSON.parse's last-value behavior. YAML duplicates are rejected.
+The full provider and these missing local contracts remain separate gates.
+
+The primary SKILL example uses `pullRequestUrl` to satisfy the output-name
+schema. The guide's top-level skeleton containing `[...]` is intentionally
+incomplete and is not an executable worked example.
+
+Installation is selective staging only. Preserve the prior version and hashes;
+rollback uses the previous immutable tree. Do not push a workflow merely to
+test this validator: default-branch files may be synced by the provider.
